 "interpretations": [
  "[\ud574\uc11d] I-1 AJ-1/2: 'F1 \uacc4\uc218' = harness fits.t1[key]['F1'].coef even when the accepted form is F2/F3; NA_FORM only when the harness label is FORM_INADEQUATE_* (no form accepted). The chosen form is reported per mode.",
  "[\ud574\uc11d] I-2 AJ-1/3: a missing / unusable boot, fit or point (SM_NOT_REALIZED, < 4 cells, absent key) -> NA_POINTS (\u00a71-9 names NA_POINTS for AJ-3/AJ-4 only; reused for AJ-1/AJ-2 missing inputs).",
  "[\ud574\uc11d] I-3 AJ-1: the D axis of (i) is D_real (tables.t1[key].D_real, \u00a71-8 'realized value'); a_16/a_64 are picked by the planned mode label D16/D64. J-A keys used: 5-part keys with cap128 only (cap-48 D44 boot, TP and resume segments excluded).",
  "[\ud574\uc11d] I-4 AJ-1 (iii): BWD_UNRESOLVED / BWD_ESTIMATOR_SPLIT are evaluated separately for sub-verdict (i) and (ii); an NA on either side gives no comparison label (reason recorded), not a new label.",
  "[\ud574\uc11d] I-5 AJ-1 (iii): the decode_fwd_gpu_ms F1 is refit with the harness ct_fit.fit_t1 on the cells that have both a VALID S_eng median and a gpu_ms median, x = actual ctx (same rule as the S_eng fit, >= 4 cells).",
  "[\ud574\uc11d] I-6 AJ-1 (iv): W = analytic_terms.decode_step(nano9b_v2(4,27)).bytes_weights (weights + LM head, read once per step); BW_eff reported for every PD-mux mode present (D16..D64, 108u).",
  "[\ud574\uc11d] I-7 AJ-2: c_knee reported for every J-A cap128 mode with an F1 fit (incl. 108u, 108v). 'difference > 50 %' = |x1 - x2| / min(|x1|, |x2|) > 0.5 (the stricter, more-flagging reading), separately for b and c; sign flip or a zero coefficient -> unstable.",
  "[\ud574\uc11d] I-8 AJ-2 J-H1 side table and AJ-4 T1 are computed only when the J-H1 T1 W-INDEP label is WEIGHT_INDEP_HELD (AJ-4 per-term rule); slope of b(n) vs n_M = OLS over the 4 variants, all 4 required.",
  "[\ud574\uc11d] I-9 AJ-3: strict NA_POINTS -- the reference (D16) and all four non-reference D must be CONFIRMED at BOTH L 32,768 and 65,536 (10 points); otherwise no theta' label.",
  "[\ud574\uc11d] I-10 AJ-3: lag_share is checked for every used point including the reference values; if any lag_share is NA (same-boot T1 (1,2k) missing) or > 3 %, the theta' label is withheld (THETA_LAG_BOUND_EXCEEDED flag in the latter case); a withheld label counts as NA for the two-Job comparison.",
  "[\ud574\uc11d] I-11 AJ-3: no NA_FORM gate -- theta' is a log-ratio regression on points, it does not use the T2' quadratic fit.",
  "[\ud574\uc11d] I-12 AJ-3 descriptive: per-L through-origin theta' and per-L free-intercept slope for every L of the T2' grid (non-reference D CONFIRMED at that L with the reference CONFIRMED at that L).",
  "[\ud574\uc11d] I-13 AJ-4: Delta_ideal = OLS slope over n_A of the per-variant ideal time (equals the one-layer difference since analytic-v1 is linear in n_A at fixed n_A + n_M); prefill time = prefill_flops.total / 312 TFLOP/s; decode time = max(decode_step.flops / 312 TFLOP/s, decode_step.bytes_total / 2.039 TB/s) at the NOMINAL c (roofline; both parts reported).",
  "[\ud574\uc11d] I-14 AJ-4: decode 'ctx \uac04 \ucc28\uc758 \ucc28' = beta1(bs, c) - beta1(bs, 2k) per bs (and the same for Delta_ideal); the per-cell decode beta1 is reported but flagged level_includes_weight_term.",
  "[\ud574\uc11d] I-15 J-H1 keys: dummy_a{n} / 108v / cap128 T1 table and dummy_a{n} / 108v T2 table; more than one matching key -> NA_POINTS."
 ],
 "scope": {
  "AJ-1": "D <= 64 1/D compatibility and 64-108 knee only; s_108 includes the 108u (sticky OFF) vs sticky-D stream-path difference; BWD_KNEE_64_108 is not 'saturation at 80 SMs'; 'HBM saturation' wording forbidden.",
  "AJ-2": "c_knee = ratio of the whole per-request term; not evidence that the state term is visible in decode time; no layer-type reading of D differences. No label (only KNEE_COEF_UNSTABLE tag).",
  "AJ-3": "theta' is a composite of one co-resident decode and SM reduction (L >= 32k); does not support 'prefill throughput proportional to P'.",
  "AJ-4": "beta1 = total effect of a layer swap (weight bytes and KV pool included), 4 points / 2 dof, descriptive; not a separation of eta_A, eta_M."
 },
